The Security Council,

Recalling the General Framework Agreement for Peace in Bosnia and Herzegovina and the Annexes thereto (collectively the Peace Agreement, S/1995/999, Annex), as well as the relevant decisions of the Peace Implementation Council,

Reaffirming that the primary responsibility for the further successful implementation of the Peace Agreement lies with all the authorities in Bosnia and Herzegovina themselves,

Reaffirming provisions concerning the High Representative as set out in its previous resolutions,

1. Agrees to the designation of Mr. Christian Schmidt as High Representative for Bosnia and Herzegovina, following the decision of the Steering Board of the Peace Implementation Council of 27 May 2021, until 31 July 2022;

2. Decides that, in view of the significant progress achieved by the parties in Bosnia and Herzegovina, the powers described in the Conclusions of the Peace Implementation Conference held in Bonn on 9 and 10 December 1997 (the Bonn powers) are no longer required in the context of the civilian implementation of the Peace Agreement;

3. Supports the closure of the Office of the High Representative on 31 July 2022, as previously discussed within the Steering Board of the Peace Implementation Council;

4. Decides to remain seized of the matter.

